er designated following departure of interim postholder","lead":"The Section 151 Officer is the council's principal statutory officer for financial administration and governance. Continuity of experienced financial leadership is important to assessing the council's financial stability and proper resource stewardship.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"DESIGNATION OF SECTION 151 OFFICER","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31432/31432.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Multiple governance mechanisms for Harlow Regeneration Partnership remain outstanding and overdue","lead":"Governance weaknesses over a major regeneration partnership create risk around decision-making, accountability and compliance. Sustained delays in implementing basic governance mechanisms suggest the partnership is not being actively managed.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Former tenant arrears require additional dedicated resource for recovery","lead":"Former tenant arrears represents uncollected housing revenue. The need for dedicated additional resource suggests the issue is significant enough to require capacity beyond existing staffing.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Council","paper_title":"DESIGNATION OF SECTION 151 OFFICER","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31432/31432.pdf","headline":"Experienced Section 151 Officer designated following departure of interim postholder","detail":"Mike Curtis, who served as S151 Officer at Kensington and Chelsea and Islington councils, is designated as Harlow's Section 151 Officer from 28 September 2026. The current interim S151 Officer's contract ends 25 September 2026. The council notes the appointment is interim, reflecting Local Government Reorganisation uncertainty in the market for experienced senior officers, and confirms it can meet the cost from existing resources. A two-day weekend gap is covered by Tracie Langley, the Executive Director/Head of Paid Service, who has previous S151 experience.","category":"people","matters":"The Section 151 Officer is the council's principal statutory officer for financial administration and governance. Continuity of experienced financial leadership is important to assessing the council's financial stability and proper resource stewardship.","figures":"Current interim contract ends 25 September 2026; new appointment from 28 September 2026","quote":"Mike is a highly experienced senior local government finance professional with significant experience operating as a Section 151 Officer. Most recently, he served as Executive Director of Resources and Section 151 Officer at the Royal Borough of Kensington and Chelsea.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit & Standards Committee","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","headline":"Multiple governance mechanisms for Harlow Regeneration Partnership remain outstanding and overdue","detail":"Five audit recommendations relating to HRP governance remain unimplemented after multiple deadline revisions: the investment plan (originally due April 2026, revised to September 2026), key decision documentation, monitoring officer board participation, terms of reference review, and data sharing agreement. The HRP Board has not met recently despite these outstanding governance requirements.","category":"governance","matters":"Governance weaknesses over a major regeneration partnership create risk around decision-making, accountability and compliance. Sustained delays in implementing basic governance mechanisms suggest the partnership is not being actively managed.","figures":"5 recommendations overdue, investment plan original deadline April 2026 revised to September 2026","quote":"The HRP governance arrangements should be strengthened to ensure adherence to the governance structure","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit & Standards Committee","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","headline":"Former tenant arrears require additional dedicated resource for recovery","detail":"The council has requested an additional dedicated resource for 12 months to oversee recovery and management of former tenant debts. This resource request is currently under consideration by the Executive Leadership Team, indicating the council views former tenant arrears as a material collection issue.","category":"income","matters":"Former tenant arrears represents uncollected housing revenue. The need for dedicated additional resource suggests the issue is significant enough to require capacity beyond existing staffing.","figures":"1 additional FTE requested for 12 months (to 31 March 2027)","quote":"Additional resource (e.g. agency workers) should be requested of the Section 151 Officer as taking on temporary staff may help address Former Tenant Arrears","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit & Standards Committee","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","headline":"Commercial property rent for one site not invoiced until 8 quarters after billing dates","detail":"Quarterly rent for one commercial property was not raised until after the fact, covering 8 quarters of arrears dating back to September 2023. This was attributed to a legacy case handling error. The council is now implementing a checklist process and reviewing all 2025/26 commercial property debts to prevent recurrence.","category":"income","matters":"Failure to invoice rent promptly affects cash collection timing and suggests weaknesses in commercial property financial management. Eight quarters of delay represents a material cash flow impact.","figures":"8 quarters of rent involved, arrears dating to September 2023","quote":"the quarterly rent for 1 Slackbury Hatch was raised for 8 quarters dating back to September 2023.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit & Standards Committee","paper_title":"App B IA Recommendation tracker","paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31414/31414.pdf","headline":"Contracts in housing operations starting without being signed","detail":"Audit found that work was commencing without contracts being signed first. The director acknowledges this was a historic issue but training on Contract Standing Orders remains overdue (originally due 30 June, now 30 October) and is pending leader review of the contract commencement process.","category":"governance","matters":"Unsigned contracts represent a material control weakness in procurement and creates legal and financial exposure for the council.","figures":"High priority finding, overdue since 30 June 2026","quote":"Ensuring contracts are signed before work commences on site.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Harlow","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Experienced Section 151 Officer designated following departure of interim postholder","lead":"The Section 151 Officer is the council's principal statutory officer for financial administration and governance. Continuity of experienced financial leadership is important to assessing the council's financial stability and proper resource stewardship.","also":["14 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":15,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"DESIGNATION OF SECTION 151 OFFICER","top_paper_url":"https://harlow.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31432/31432.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":101,"news_drafts_total":3}}